Subject: read VSI ssh's exit status as success on VMS

VSI's ssh client exits with a VMS status; waitpid() keeps its low byte,
27 when the remote command ended 0, so every transfer over ssh ended with
rsync reporting the child's failure. vms_child_status() maps it.

--- a/main.c	2026-11-06 14:45:32.460750538 +0000
+++ b/main.c	2026-11-06 14:45:32.480109969 +0000
@@ -1401,6 +1401,10 @@
 
 	if (waitpid(child, &st, 0) == -1)
 		err(ERR_WAITPID, "waitpid");
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/* VSI ssh's VMS exit status, as rsync should read it (vms_spawn.c). */
+	st = vms_child_status(st, args);
+#endif
 
 	/*
 	 * If the child exited abnormally then use its exit status as our exit
